8. Implementation Recommendations According to the Objective
Objective: Optimized SEO + GEO Blog Post
Recommended Structure:

H1 Title: include the main keyword + a question or benefit formulation
Introduction: answer the main question directly in 2-3 sentences (BLUF)
Table of contents with internal anchors (structure signal for LLMs)
Body: H2 per sub-theme, H3 for details. Alternate short paragraphs, lists, tables
Structured FAQ at the end of the article (FAQPage schema): 3 to 5 questions that prospects actually ask
Cited and linked sources
Article Schema with author, date, image

Checklist before publication:
[ ] Search intent is identified and respected
[ ] Main answer is in the first 100 words
[ ] At least one dated and sourced figure per section
[ ] Article + FAQPage schemas implemented
[ ] Internal linking to the pillar page and 2-3 related articles
[ ] Meta title (< 60 characters) and meta description (< 155 characters) written
[ ] Images optimized (WebP format, descriptive alt text)
[ ] Core Web Vitals score in the green on mobile

Objective: Product / Service SEO Page
Recommended Structure:
H1: main benefit + keyword (not just the product name)
Short description: what it is, who it is for, result obtained
Proof: figures, customer testimonials, logos, case studies
Functional details: list of features with associated benefits
FAQ on common objections (FAQPage schema)
Clear and repeated CTA

E-E-A-T Signals on a Product Page:
Number of clients, countries, years of existence
Verified reviews with names and companies
Certifications, partnerships, known integrations

9. AI Content — Publication Rules
AI-generated content must be validated and enriched by a human expert before publication. Google detects and penalizes raw AI content without added value.
What needs to be added to AI-generated content:
Field data that only a practitioner can provide
Concrete examples named with dates and results
An expert angle or opinion that cannot be found elsewhere
Proofreading to remove generic phrasing and typical AI turns of phrase

What remains prohibited:
AI content published without proofreading
Keyword stuffing
Copying or paraphrasing existing articles

10. Common Errors to Avoid
Error: No schema.org
Impact: Not citable by LLMs, fewer Google rich snippets.
Correction: Implement Article + FAQPage as a priority.
Error: Homepage as the target for all links
Impact: Poorly distributed authority, deep pages under-ranked.
Correction: Topical internal linking to key pages.
Error: Content without clear intent
Impact: Google does not know who to rank → poor position.
Correction: One page = one intent = one main keyword.
Error: Ignoring mobile
Impact: Degraded ranking (mobile-first indexing).
Correction: Systematically test and correct on mobile.
Error: Blocking GPTBot / ClaudeBot in robots.txt
Impact: Invisible to LLMs.
Correction: Check and allow AI crawlers.
Error: Raw AI content published without enrichment
Impact: Google algorithmic penalty, not citable.
Correction: Mandatory validation + expert enrichment.
Error: Updating positions but not the content
Impact: Content ages, loses GEO authority.
Correction: Quarterly content audit + data update.
Error: No author page
Impact: Missing E-E-A-T signal → less cited by AIs.
Correction: Author page + Person schema on each article.
Error: Targeting low-volume keywords on a new site
Impact: No traffic despite efforts.
Correction: Start with the long tail, then move up in competitiveness.
Error: No external presence (press, LinkedIn, newsletter)
Impact: GEO authority limited to the site alone.
Correction: Distribute content on other channels.

